{"body":"## Summary\n\nFull feature-parity restoration against **pi v0.81.1** (`earendil-works/pi`, tag `v0.81.1`), driven by a complete audit of pi's entire `packages/coding-agent` tree (not just the recent 0.81.1 delta — historical port gaps included). Four parallel audit passes (core, interactive TUI, shell/extensions, provider-surface/SDK/docs) produced ~30 findings; everything below is implemented. Deliberate exclusions (approved): Atomic's verbatim compaction, workflows/subagents/mcp/web-access/intercom builtins, branding, the 600s HTTP idle-timeout default (pi-compatible serialized values are now accepted), and grep-tool compat aliases (tool no longer exists in Atomic).\n\n## Login/provider surface (the headline gaps)\n\n- **Qwen Token Plan hidden from `/login`** — root cause: `isApiKeyLoginProvider()` used the display-name map as an auth allowlist. API-key options now derive from pi-ai provider auth metadata, restoring `qwen-token-plan`, `qwen-token-plan-cn`, `radius`, and `github-copilot` API-key login; display names added as overrides only.\n- **`/login <provider>`** direct routing (id/display-name resolution, method chooser, prefiltered selector fallback) + fuzzy provider autocomplete + argument hint.\n- Provider-owned login **info links** (`AuthInfoLink`) carried through the oauth bridge and rendered as terminal hyperlinks.\n- Preferred defaults: `radius: auto`, `nvidia`, `zai-coding-cn`.\n\n## llama.cpp builtin extension (`/login llama.cpp`, `/llama`)\n\n- Full port of pi's hidden inline extension: router client (URL normalization, `/models[?reload=1]`, load/unload, SSE progress + catalog polling, non-router rejection), provider (`LLAMA_BASE_URL`/`LLAMA_API_KEY`, loaded-models-only catalog, context/output caps, modality detection), `/llama` manager UI, and the Hugging Face GGUF browser (token discovery chain, quantization/shard enumeration, `Q4_K_M` preference, gated-repo warning).\n- Named/hidden `InlineExtension` descriptors (`<inline:llama.cpp>`, hidden from startup lists) wired through resource loading, package/config commands, and the isolated engine runtime.\n- Custom provider API-key **login/check/resolve** contract with credential `env` metadata.\n- **Isolated-engine auth bridge** (extensions load only in the engine child): the RPC model catalog syncs `customAuthProviders` metadata to the host, and a `login_provider` RPC executes custom logins in the child with prompts routed through the existing engine input bridge, cancellation propagation, shared credential storage, and post-login model refresh. Generic — no provider-specific logic.\n\n## Settings/config/CLI\n\n`httpProxy` setting; `httpIdleTimeoutMs` accepts `\"disabled\"`/numeric strings; package `autoload: false` project deltas (incl. workflows resources); `deferredToolsMode: \"kimi\"`; `oauth: \"radius\"` custom gateways in models.json; `atomic config -l` with global/project scope switching; self-update advisory notes + exact-version pinning; Windows quarantine cleanup on ordinary startup.\n\n## Extension events & SDK parity\n\n`before_provider_headers` and `agent_settled` events; custom session-entry renderers (`registerEntryRenderer` + `entry_appended` + live/restored TUI rendering); native `registerProvider(Provider)` overload; public `ModelRuntime` facade accepted by the SDK; root exports: `readStoredCredential`, `InlineExtension`, session context helpers, event/renderer types.\n\n## Interactive UX & accounting\n\nCtrl+X copy-last-message; clipboard text fallback on intercepted paste (+ native `getText()`); footer git branch/session name/extension statuses/`xp` marker (with ANSI-safe sanitization — statuses keep their colors); output-padding `/settings` item; idle status shrink placeholder; cache-miss waste accounting with `showCacheMissNotices` setting + `/settings` toggle + `/session` reporting; usage totals with tool/summary buckets and per-model `/session` cost breakdown; first-run theme picker + analytics opt-in (`enableAnalytics`/`trackingId`, storage only — nothing is transmitted).\n\n## Docs & changelog\n\nNew `docs/llama-cpp.md`; providers.md (Radius/xAI subscriptions, Qwen `/login` consistency, dynamic catalogs + `models-store.json`, provider-scoped credential `env`); models.md (`oauth` field, native API surface clarification); settings/keybindings/packages/extensions/sdk pages; comprehensive CHANGELOG entries.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Full unit suite green (**3,964+ tests**, up from 3,919), typecheck, lint, `check:file-length`, `docs:check`, `--help`/`--list-models` smoke — plus new focused suites: `login-provider-parity`, `llama-extension-parity`, `pi-parity-group-{3,4,5}`, `rpc-provider-login`.\n- Real tmux E2E session evidence in PR comment (leniency as agreed: no qwen/llama credentials available, so evidence shows the surfaces exist and the flows execute up to real credential validation).\n\nAssistant-model: Claude Fable 5\n","files":[{"path":"packages/coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md","additions":22,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/docs.json","additions":2,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md","additions":56,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/keybindings.md","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/llama-cpp.md","additions":70,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/models.md","additions":8,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md","additions":4,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/providers.md","additions":37,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/sdk.md","additions":18,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md","additions":19,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"packages/coding-agent/src/cli/args.ts","additions":2,"